From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave out the Asset Library

The editor's AssetLib screen and the project manager's Asset Library
tab browse Godot's asset store, whose assets are made and checked for
Godot's own releases. Purr isn't Godot, so it shouldn't present
Godot's store as its own. Both depend on
AssetLibraryEditorPlugin::is_available(), which now returns false, as
Godot already does on the web editor.

Addons still install by copying them into a project's addons/ folder.

Test: open the project manager and the editor; neither shows an Asset
Library tab.

Upstream: Purr only.
---
 godot/editor/asset_library/asset_library_editor_plugin.cpp | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/godot/editor/asset_library/asset_library_editor_plugin.cpp b/godot/editor/asset_library/asset_library_editor_plugin.cpp
index 1e8d0db3..b0e20fb3 100644
--- a/godot/editor/asset_library/asset_library_editor_plugin.cpp
+++ b/godot/editor/asset_library/asset_library_editor_plugin.cpp
@@ -2405,13 +2405,8 @@ EditorAssetLibrary::EditorAssetLibrary(bool p_templates_only) {
 ///////
 
 bool AssetLibraryEditorPlugin::is_available() {
-#ifdef WEB_ENABLED
-	// Asset Store can't work on Web editor for now as most assets are sourced
-	// directly from GitHub which does not set CORS.
+	// Purr leaves out Godot's Asset Library: it's Godot's store, for Godot's releases.
 	return false;
-#else
-	return StreamPeerTLS::is_available() && !Engine::get_singleton()->is_recovery_mode_hint();
-#endif
 }
 
 void AssetLibraryEditorPlugin::make_visible(bool p_visible) {
